  "sections": [
    {
      "heading": "This, that, that over there",
      "body": "Spanish has three distances. The demonstrative agrees with the noun in gender and number.",
      "table": {
        "head": [
          "",
          "near me (this)",
          "near you (that)",
          "far from both (that over there)"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "masc. sing.",
            "*este*",
            "*ese*",
            "*aquel*"
          ],
          [
            "fem. sing.",
            "*esta*",
            "*esa*",
            "*aquella*"
          ],
          [
            "masc. plural",
            "*estos*",
            "*esos*",
            "*aquellos*"
          ],
          [
            "fem. plural",
            "*estas*",
            "*esas*",
            "*aquellas*"
          ]
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "heading": "Using them",
      "body": "Before a noun: *Esta camisa es bonita.* (This shirt is pretty.) *¿Cuánto cuestan esos zapatos?* (How much are those shoes?)\n\nOn their own, when the noun is clear: *¿Te gusta esta? — No, prefiero esa.* (Do you like this one? — No, I prefer that one.)\n\nFor something unknown or an idea, use the neuter forms *esto* (this), *eso* (that), *aquello* (that over there): *¿Qué es esto?* (What's this?) *Eso es interesante.* They never go before a noun."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Colours",
      "body": "Colours are adjectives and go after the noun. Those ending in *-o* have four forms (*rojo, roja, rojos, rojas*); the others have two (*verde, verdes; azul, azules*). *Rosa* and *naranja* often don't change at all: *unos zapatos rosa*.\n\nTo ask: *¿De qué color es?* (What colour is it?)"
    },
    {
      "heading": "In the shop",
      "body": "- *¿Puedo probarme esta camisa?* — Can I try on this shirt?\n- *¿Qué talla usa?* — What size do you wear? (clothes) · *¿Qué número calza?* — What size shoe?\n- *Me queda grande / pequeño.* — It's too big / small on me.\n- *Me lo llevo.* — I'll take it."
    }
  ],
